      "title": "Letterboxd review of Catch Me If You Can",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Catch Me If You Can\"] Action!: The Campy, The Violent and The Plot Twist - Sommers' CampAhh, the 80s, when you had 30 somethings playing high schoolers. Before he had Brendan Fraser fighting mummies and Hugh Jackman hunting vampires, Stephen Sommers blast into the scene with his 80s high school version of Need For Speed. A story of love where the heart beats vroom vroom. Furthermore, students in the school cared for it to the extent that they were willing to break the law to save it from closing. In my days, that would be a motive of celebration where we would gather dance around and sing along to the lyrics of \"Tu",
