      "title": "Letterboxd review of Catch Me If You Can",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Catch Me If You Can\"] This is Stephen Sommers’ debut feature and it’s like the love child of AMERICAN GRAFFITI And THREE O’CLOCK HIGH or something. Features a group of kids trying to raise money to keep their school from shutting down and getting involved in car street racing. Has a Tangerine Dream score and an interesting but sturdy dramatic build to one heck of a final race. Also, Geoffrey Lewis is great as the juke box owning Principal of this down and out high school in dire need of $200,000 and M. Emmet Walsh is great as Johnny Phatmun aka “the Fat Man” who runs a gambling syndicate and hates to lose.",
