      "title": "Letterboxd review of Catch Me If You Can",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Catch Me If You Can\"] Winter trash 24/2577. 3/7 - Watch an action movie from 1989.Catch Me If You Can isn’t winning any Oscars, but it’s a delightfully cheesy time capsule of late ‘80s absurdity that I can’t fully hate. Matt Lattanzi, who’s biggest claim to fame is being Olivia Newton-John’s ex, stumbles through this teen drag-racing flick with the charisma of a mullet in a windstorm. He plays Dylan, a high schooler who bets his car in illegal street races to save his school’s funding, because apparently that’s how economics works in Minnesota. The plot’s thin, and the dialogue sounds like it was written by a caffe",
