      "title": "Letterboxd review of Catch Me If You Can",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Catch Me If You Can\"] The first movie directed by overhated studio schlockmeister Stephen Sommers is this John Hughes-esque zany high school comedy that no one ever saw, but they should've! It's lively and winning, and knows how to amplify hijinks for cinematic value while giving the characters some developmental anchorage. Sure if you squint it looks like a non-musical \"Grease\" (bad boy and wholesome girl join forces, lots of '50s nostalgia, drag race finale), but what doesn't? Matt Lattanzi is our hero, sporting some fake-greaser Travolta charm (and not just cuz he resembles him physically, or because Lattanzi co",
